the Palestinian armed group Islamic  Jihad says a ceasefire has been agreed  with Israel in Gaza after two days of  cross-border fighting these are live  pictures from Gaza where calm appears to  have been restored Egypt has been  mediating between the two sides the  escalation began after a senior leader  of Islamic Jihad was killed in an  Israeli airstrike well Rob Matheson  joins us on the phone now from West  Jerusalem Rob so what more details have  emerged about this ceasefire well we've  had no official confirmation down yet  for here in Israel that this is five  ceasefire is in place but it is being  widely reported in the media it is  expected to have gone in has it have  begun at about all 5:30 local time this  morning we have teams both in Gaza on  both the Israeli border with Gaza the  team in Gaza has been telling us that  since that time they have heard rockets  and explosions inside the Gaza the team  on the Israeli border with Gaza has been  saying that sirens have been sounding in  areas which are close to that border now  we should stress that whenever there has  been a sea star in the past this is the  pattern that does occur that it takes  time for the details and the  notifications of the ceasefire to be put  into place to calculate those and  therefore if there is a lessening in  attacks excuse me it usually takes a  little bit of time for that to take  place as far as the details of the  actual ceasefire itself a concern we're  hearing that Islamic Jihad has agreed to  stop firing rockets into Israel and it's  also going to make sure that protests  along the Gaza border are peaceful for  its part Israel says that it will no  longer do targeted killings has  committed to stop shooting protesters at  border fence interestingly there has not  yet been any mention of one key  requirement that the Islamic Jihad group  had put in place which was to ease the  blockade that is currently on Gaza this  Israel has put very strict controls over  who and what can be moved across the  border back and forth between Gaza  and Israel they say the user extractions  are necessary for security reasons to  stop the possibility of technology and  weapons and individuals being able to  get into Gaza to be able to build  armaments for the armed groups that are  inside the Gaza Strip but at the moment  the death toll in Gaza standing at about  thirty two there were air strikes prior  to the ceasefire being put in place and  rockets were being fired out of Gaza  particularly around midnight we heard  that there was a very significantly  large barrage of rockets that were aimed  into Israel predominantly towards Tel  Aviv but at the moment we're just  waiting to see when this ceasefire is  officially acknowledged and if it will  actually take time to die down all right  now Rob Mathison there in West Jerusalem  Rob thank you
 

